c.execute("update paper_boundary_audit set status='full_paper_boundaries_verified',observed_units=42,evidence=?,checked_at=? where file_id=3137",('All nine physical pages inspected: cover p1, Q1-Q41 pp2-8 and separate Q42 p9. Q28 continues pp5-6. Lettered/extra requests remain whole parents; closing TeX marker is not a task. No omitted independent top-level item; navigation references to other contests are not automatically equivalent source records.',w.now()))
notes={2:'Ideal flexible homogeneous line with negligible bending stiffness is a declared approximation. Energy-conserving versus inelastic transfer at the bend must be distinguished; circle approximation limits the radius estimate.',3:'Friction model intentionally has negligible kinetic and very large static coefficients. Based-on IPhO credit does not prove an exact alias of a specific uninspected older problem.',7:'Rope torsion energy expressly zero; use contact helical geometry and stated Coulomb friction. Rod mass cancels some gravity timescales but must be retained if contact model changes.',8:'Postcollision debris speed/energy loss is not uniquely given; envelope is a parametric Newtonian conic family.',9:'Force integral may diverge for some n inside material. Range/cutoff and hollow-shell theorem failure must be checked rather than import inverse-square formula.',10:'Material density not supplied; base width parameterized by density. Torque-balance construction is prescribed, not a beam-deflection question.',11:'Specify patch areal density and pretension/force matching, outer radius and clamped boundary; no full flexural plate law implied by the stated membrane model.',12:'No fan endurance test performed. Calibrated wear/monitoring/survival method is a proposed measurement protocol, not a fabricated lifetime.',13:'At static equilibrium kinetic energy vanishes; Euler homogeneity gives nU=0 when n nonzero and no excluded external constraints. n=0/constraints/offset constants are explicit counterexamples.',14:'No bubble experiment performed. Interface tension/wetting and possible film rupture are measurable model parameters, not invented observations.',15:'Coastal height is a rough resonance/geometric estimate, not a simulated quantitative Saint-Malo/Saint-Lawrence hydrodynamic result.',16:'gamma=1 is an idealized isothermal perturbation rule; exponential hydrostatic profile alone lacks central wave dynamical equations.',18:'Fixed spatial sphere with explicit Poisson equation, not curved gravitational spacetime. Two-circle geometry must be declared for separation/overlap degeneracies.',19:'Shared rotating-sphere model with 2006 Q19, but different printed requests; not exact equivalence. Electron free-carrier approximation explicitly supplied.',21:'Suggested Jeng paper optional; graph is completely specified and standard Kirchhoff law suffices.',22:'Point-dipole whole-space claim needs distributional source terms/contact contributions, not just source-free equality away from origin. Retarded classical EM is operational scope.',23:'Atmospheric index/temperature profile is a modelling parameter; separated-image condition needs nonmonotonic ray mapping, not a specified fluid evolution law.',25:'Actual roof drawing sets spacer orientation and sheet dimensions; material refractive index, observer distance and roof tilt need declared values.',27:'Creation physics expressly excluded; choose albedo/thermal redistribution assumptions for Europa and other bodies, not a detailed climate model.',28:'F_k supplied is a four-force formula; the relation to three-force/proper time and rest-mass evolution is not. Reference to named covariant theory does not supply that machinery.',29:'f=v/b explicitly given. Stellar masses, velocity distribution and minimum physical pericentre require declared realistic parameters. This asks rate of produced frequency-band encounters, not detector amplitude/SNR.',30:'Particle action genuinely supplied, but field action/stress tensor/equivalence and covariant dynamics are not. Do not replace the whole task with its mechanical subpart.',31:'Dimension, metric and how springs measure distance are not fixed; an embedded surface model and a general intrinsic model need not give the same minimal arrangement/force.',32:'Declare stationary chain and free radon escape surface. Same sphere diffusion model as 2008 Q32 but a different direct-versus-inverse task, not an exact printed reprint.',33:'Breakup distance/time and relative fragment direction are not specified; centre trajectory may be parametric or nonunique. Absorbed momentum is explicitly neglected as a toy idealization. No fabricated unique numerical orbit.',34:'Suggested Slonczewski 1963 paper primary abstract inspected, full PDF reports 401 Unauthorized. No bypass or full-paper inspection claimed; incomplete phonon model/quantum rules remain explicit.',36:'Conditional phase evolution and metric are supplied; missing proper-time definition/reduced-state rule are acknowledged precisely. No false assertion that evolution is absent.',37:'All stated gates and singlet are supplied; measurement Born/partial-state/no-disturbance rules are not operationally defined.',38:'A finite self-terminating beam is not supplied by ordinary optical force alone. The requested nonlinear/confinement mechanism is unspecified, so no fabricated threshold.',39:'Exact or controlled analytical approximation requested; simulation alone explicitly called an illustration. Need clarify update ordering/simultaneous events in a chosen mathematical convention.',40:'No room measurements or actual airing schedule tested. Heat capacity, pollution generation, exchange rates and discomfort objective are parameters to estimate/measure.',41:'No operational intelligence definition or behavioral dataset supplied. Geometry may suggest organization but cannot uniquely certify intelligence; the limitation is itself accessible by logical counterexamples.',42:'Viewing direction/binocular apparent-image convention and depth/height/index are parameters. Remote 1991 story reference does not provide extra required data.'}
